Histogram shows how many values fall in each range.
What is a Histogram?
A histogram is a graphical representation that organizes a group of data points into specified ranges, called bins.
 It is the go-to tool for understanding the "underlying frequency distribution" of a continuous variable.
Think of it as taking a pile of data and sorting it into buckets to see where the "peaks" and "valleys" are.

  distplot is univariate plot.


KDE (Kernel Density Estimate)

KDE is a smooth curve over histogram.
It estimates the probability density function (PDF).
Example shape

       /\ 
      /  \
     /    \

If it looks like bell shape, distribution may be Gaussian.
